Provenance of the files below engine/protocol/
----------------------------------------------

- spec/ (normative specification) and proto/ (Protocol Buffers schema)
  were written from scratch for impluvium. They are not derived from the
  schema files, generated types or source code inherited elsewhere in this
  repository. They contain no third-party source code; the only
  third-party material is the data listed under "Third-party material".

- The schema imports google/protobuf/timestamp.proto, a well-known type
  that the Protocol Buffers toolchain provides. It is referenced, not
  copied into this tree.

- The specification implements, and refers to, published constructions
  and standards without copying their text: the DSSE pre-authentication
  encoding (secure-systems-lab/dsse, protocol version 1), Ed25519
  (RFC 8032), HKDF (RFC 5869), SHA-256 (FIPS 180-4), MD5 (RFC 1321, used
  only to describe how a constant table was produced), BLAKE3, FastCDC
  (Xia et al., 2020), the Connect protocol, the Protocol Buffers binary
  and JSON encodings, Server-Sent Events (WHATWG HTML Living Standard),
  the WHATWG URL Standard, the OAuth 2.0 device authorization grant
  (RFC 8628), Unicode 16.0.0 character data and the HTTP specifications
  cited in the chapters.

- The package facades in engine/crates/{protocol,client}, the TypeScript
  package facade, local generator configurations, xtask and their tests
  were written from scratch for impluvium under 0BSD. No inherited
  application code or experimental implementation was copied into them.

- The generated Rust message and service trees and ts/src/generated are
  produced only from proto/ by the pinned local buffa, Connect and
  protobuf-es plugins. Keep any notices emitted by those generators.
  Generator sources, runtime libraries and Google well-known-type sources
  are not vendored here. Their licenses remain separate from this project's
  own sources; resolved dependencies require their own license review.

- The hash/chunk benchmark records its selective 0BSD source adaptations,
  algorithm attribution and external dependencies in
  benchmarks/hashchunk/PROVENANCE.md. No additional third-party source is copied.

- The reference checker, synthetic protocol cases and integration configuration
  are project work under 0BSD. Field-level numerical origins and calculation
  status are recorded in testdata/ and conformance/reference/FORMAT.md.
  Installed compiler, type and hash packages retain their own licenses and
  are checked through the resolved dependency graph.

Third-party material
--------------------

spec/manifest.md, section 9 (FastCDC chunking), and
testdata/fastcdc-constants.json contain the 256-entry gear table and two mask constants of the Rust crate fastcdc, version 5.0.0, module
v2020 (https://github.com/nlfiedler/fastcdc-rs, crate archive SHA-256
0431c3132902a1bed6fe77dcfa5d03844e083f263b81288246a2d43dd7d4b2ad). The gear
table values are the first 8 bytes of the MD5 digests of 64-byte strings
whose bytes all equal the table index, and can be regenerated from that rule.
The cut procedure is described in the specification in its own words,
