Additional numerical test data
------------------------------

The following material keeps its third-party terms; it is not relicensed as
project-owned 0BSD work. testdata/foreign/SOURCES.json records the original
source and excerpt digests. Corpus origin records identify each selected
input and expected value. No third-party implementation source is copied.

- testdata/unicode16.json contains numerical mappings derived from Unicode
  16.0.0 UnicodeData.txt (SHA-256
  ff58e5823bd095166564a006e47d111130813dcf8bf234ef79fa51a870edb48f)
  and CaseFolding.txt (SHA-256
  6f1f9c588eb4a5c718d9e8f93b782685e5c7fec872cf05e8e6878053599e09bb).
  Source: https://www.unicode.org/Public/16.0.0/ucd/ . These derived data
  retain Unicode License V3, reproduced in
  testdata/foreign/UNICODE-LICENSE-V3.txt.

- Selected HKDF-SHA-256 and pure Ed25519 numerical known answers in
  testdata/primitives-000.json come from RFC 5869 Appendix A and RFC 8032
  section 7.1: https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc5869 and
  https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc8032 . RFC text and example code are
  excluded. The publications' IETF Trust notices remain separate:
  https://trustee.ietf.org/trust-legal-provisions/ . Each corpus origin
  identifies its source digest and selected value.

- Selected individual SHA-256/SHA-512 message/digest pairs in
  testdata/primitives-000.json come from NIST CAVP Secure Hashing test files:
  https://csrc.nist.gov/projects/cryptographic-algorithm-validation-program/secure-hashing .
  Source digests and pair selectors identify the exact inputs. No complete
  NIST test file is redistributed. The source copyright statement is
  identified in SOURCES.json by SHA-256
  fe9e90da227416b8690264d7a93a546a8e81487514134f636674fc475108c11d.
  Source information was recorded on 2026-11-16; these numerical pairs
  are separate from project-owned code.

- Selected unkeyed 32-byte BLAKE3 answers in testdata/primitives-000.json
  come from the upstream test_vectors/test_vectors.json data (source
  SHA-256 dcb91ea8accc77e6d6e632af7cdc1a99a9f3ae78cf648da595c7d064db32f624):
  https://github.com/BLAKE3-team/BLAKE3 . They retain CC0-1.0, reproduced
